      <div class="title-divider"></div>
      <p><strong>Best time:</strong> October and November give the clearest views, and March to May brings rhododendron blooms. See our <a href="/best-season-for-kokhe-danda-trek">month-by-month guide to the best time for Kokhe Danda</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>Cost:</strong> the trek costs $350 to $410 per person depending on group size. It includes private transport, meals, accommodation, guide and porter. See the cost table.</p>
      <p><strong>Getting there:</strong> we drive from Pokhara to Banau via Kushma in about 2.5 hours, then walk to Haljure. The trek ends at Mallaj, with a taxi back to Pokhara via Kushma.</p>
      <p><strong>Kokhe Danda or Poon Hill?</strong> Read <a href="/kokhe-danda-trek-alternative-to-poon-hill">why Kokhe Danda is a better alternative to Poon Hill</a>. Short on time? Try the <a href="/short-kokhe-danda-trek">Short Kokhe Danda Trek</a>, or extend your trip with the <a href="/multiple-viewpoints-trek">Multiple Viewpoints Trek</a>.</p>
